  "setting": "target-side (kd == kt) codebook VALUE-format QAT on 2-bit nested d-sweep ckpts; weight index bits unchanged. Student = copy of all kt codebooks with STE fake-quant at stage_fmts (one fp16 scale per codebook), init = fmt2b rounding-only copy. variant refresh10: fake-quant scales re-searched (MSE) every 10 steps and once more before baking (--qat_refresh 10, script default); variant fixgrid: searched once at init (= the rounding-only grid) and kept through training and bake (--qat_refresh 0). refresh10 bakes can land on a re-searched grid the latent was not trained on (d8 mix_int4-int8: train-window TV 0.126 after bake vs ~0.074 during training, /data/lsh/results_accept/qat2b/diag); per-row scales trainable (stored fp32 in the copy, cast to bf16 in the forward). Teacher = unmodified bf16-codebook target (set_k(use_draft=False); bit-exact check vs plain target logits recorded in train.teacher_check). Codes frozen.",
